  "boundaries": [
    "All selected original GSFT proofs are separately indexed and bound to their exact original envelope/BASIS/GSRP; missing proof or incorrect carried result refuses.",
    "Ordinary plan authority checks remain. Original lower/parent and already-covered target anchors must be authenticated by the complete generation; unpublished targets never become published ancestry.",
    "The actual native fixture has two different peer intentions on non-longest source owners, a real allocated proposer ballot, and exact proposed generations for a holder and nonholder. It verifies unchanged native journals on guarded selection.",
    "A separate Java case uses a published longest prefix to verify covered-target ancestry without inventing a carried tail. Conditional malformed-source ownership occurs only in rejection tests.",
    "The first original-first reader found an omitted allocator call in test preparation. The corrected fixture uses actual reserveCounter; earlier raw evidence and logs remain retained, not relabelled.",
    "Twelve distinct final Java tests pass. The final additional conflicting-result negative is covered by the guards snapshot, which repeats three tests on identical production Java.",
    "Normal, optimized and relocated independent replay agree and reject twelve exact evidence mutations. Thirteen focused Python regressions pass in both modes; this batch does not claim a full reactor test run or new process crash qualification.",
    "Native SELECTED still refuses unresolved futures. Durable selected ownership, subsequent-source flattening, carried application/publication, complete capacity headroom and actual quorum-gated dispatch remain required.",
    "The complete offline-survivor history, learners/joint transitions and all remaining Phase 3B\u20133E gates remain OPEN. No push, public membership enablement, cloud execution or V5.2 Runner changes."
  ],
